ORSEE 3.4.1

Security:       Prevent reflected XSS in participant-search sorting and
                upload-name output.
Security:       Remove eval() for "func:" expressions in participant
                profile-field configuration.
Bugfix:         Correctly extract and store incoming email headers and
                message bodies, including non-ASCII content.
Bugfix:         Improve error handling for failed incoming-email retrieval.
Bugfix:         Make the configurable HTTP session timeout authoritative
                during session garbage collection.
Bugfix:         Fix anonymized participant data in participant-list PDFs
                attached to session emails.
Bugfix:         Correct email reply permissions for emails assigned to an
                experiment or session.
Bugfix:         Restore session-participant suggestions when assigning an
                incoming email to a participant, without duplicate entries.
Bugfix:         Avoid some undefined-variable warnings.
Bugfix:         Correct a typo in the email-retrieval setting description.


ORSEE 3.4.0

New feature:    UI migration from legacy table-based layout to responsive
                CSS/div component styling. New unified ORSEE shell and CSS
                styling system for admin and public areas. Also has dark mode.
                Public area designed mobile-first, with responsive tablet/
                desktop adaptations.
New feature:    Public content rendered via wiki-like richtext syntax
New feature:    Configurable menu editor introduced (public + admin) with
                ordering, item types, visibility rules, and custom pages.
                Menu modes: vertical, horizontal dynamic submenu,
                horizontal static submenu.
New feature:    Comprehensive participant profile layout builder,
                allowing variants based on form location and subpools,
                draft and activation. New participant profile field
                types (yes/no, date variants, phone, checkboxlist_lang).
New feature:    Full right-to-left (RTL) language support
New feature:    Support for secondary participant email.
New feature:    Query module for subscriptions in participant search.
New feature:    Selected participant fields editable in session
                participant list.
New feature:    Configurable session timeout for http sessions
New feature:    Adding auth migration status to query tool
New feature:    Convert ORSEE database tables from MyISAM to InnoDB
Bugfix:         Login js autosubmit removed (interferes with CSRF).
Bugfix:         Missing viewport meta tag.
Security:       Whitelisting $_REQUEST data 
Housekeeping:   jQuery removed. 
Housekeeping:   Onset UI assets removed. 
Housekeeping:   Font Awesome upgraded.
Housekeeping:   Running all files through php-cs-fixer (php)
                and prettier (js and css)
Housekeeping:   Update data import functions from v2 and v3.0-3.3

ORSEE 3.3.0
        Many minor and major bugfixes
        Security: Added CSRF tokens to all ORSEE forms
        Security: Session regeneration, redirect hardening,
                  cookie and email sanitization
        New feature: Integration of PHPMailer as mail backend
        New feature: OAuth2 capability for PHPMailer integration
        Updated PHPlot from version 6.2.1 to version 8.0.0.3
        Updated jQuery to version 3.7.1 and improved mobile pages
        Bugfix: Bulk mailing no longer stops when participant uses
                previously deleted language
        Bugfix: Permanent query handling fixed
        Bugfix: Language deletion fixed
        Bugfix: PHP8 compatibility fixes
        Bugfix: Replace deprecated jQuery size() with length in textext plugin
        Bugfix: Truncate cron log target to column size
        Bugfix: Avoid warnings in multi_array_sort() and uasort()
                return handling
        Misc: Fix link to documentation

ORSEE 3.2.0
        Minor and major bugfixes
        Upgrade to PHP8
	New feature: Allows different invitation email templates for 
                     different external experiment types

ORSEE 3.1.0
        Many minor and major bugfixes -> compatible with PHP7
        New feature: Bulk-anonymize participant profiles with default values
        New feature: Hide column values for some admin types
        New feature: Search for interface language in search tool
        New feature: Use internal fields in freetext search in search tool
        New feature: Use more experiment details in email texts
        New feature: Edit participant profiles from mail queue
        New feature: Download session participant list as CSV
        New feature: Change session status of multiple sessions at once
        New feature: Set experiment access restriction as default
        New feature: Restrict no-show count to sessions after specific date
        New feature: Automatically updates database when new features require
                     new language terms or new user rights
        New feature: Import participant data from csv/txt file
        New feature: Use SSL connection with external MySQL databases

